WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:16.790
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

7
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.410
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
这些故事只有我们两个亲历者才能告诉你。

8
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

9
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.090
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

10
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:24.890
Hey!
嘿！

11
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.670
We are going to business school today.
我们今天要上商学院了。

12
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.530
Oh, you guys, it's going to be so fun.
噢，伙计们，这会非常有趣。

13
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.190
We might get our frizz on.
我们可能会弄得一团糟。

14
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.840
I wouldn't know anything about that.
我对此一无所知。

15
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.400
Yeah, you're going to know everything about it because you and I have a frothing date.
是啊，你马上就会全都知道了，因为你和我有个打奶泡的约会。

16
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:41.980
I can't wait to froth with you.
我等不及要和你一起打奶泡了。

17
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.520
I'm going to chunk it at you, lady.
我要把它扔向你，女士。

18
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.620
Oh, boy.
天哪。

19
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:51.700
Guys, this is Season 3, Episode 16, written by Brent Forrester and directed by Joss Whedon.
伙计们，这是第三季第16集，由布伦特·福雷斯特编剧，乔斯·韦登执导。

20
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.500
I'm going to hit you with a summary.
我要给你们讲讲剧情概要。

21
00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:54.020
Do it.
来吧。

22
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.340
I wrote my summary really succinct today.
我今天的概要写得非常简洁。

23
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.860
Oh, it's so succinct that you had to call it out.
噢，简洁到你非得特意提出来。

24
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:02.920
I did.
没错。

25
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.240
Hey, guys, get ready for some succinct summary.
嘿，伙计们，准备好迎接简洁的概要吧。

26
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.960
Ooh, say that five times faSt.
噢，快把这句话连说五遍。

27
00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.860
Ryan brings Michael to be a guest speaker at his business school.
瑞安邀请迈克尔去他的商学院做客座讲师。

28
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.400
A bat causes mayhem at the office.
一只蝙蝠在办公室里引起了混乱。

29
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.220
Jim pretends to be turning into Dracula to prank Dwight.
吉姆假装自己正在变成德古拉来捉弄德怀特。

30
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.400
Pam shows her art at an art exhibition.
帕姆在艺术展上展示了她的画作。

31
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.440
It sounds so simple, right?
听起来很简单，对吧？

32
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.100
Four simple sentences, and yet it is not simple at all.
四句简单的句子，但实际上一点也不简单。

33
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.540
It's simple, but there's so much.
它很简单，但内容非常丰富。

34
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.220
I have one little thing to add.
我有一点要补充。

35
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:35.980
Brent says in the DVD commentary, he was handed two cards off the wall.
布伦特在DVD评论中说，他当时从墙上拿到了两张卡片。

36
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.460
You know, we've talked about how on the wall the writers have all these cards.
你知道的，我们谈过编剧们把所有这些卡片都贴在墙上。

37
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.300
Yeah.
是的。

38
00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.460
He was just handed two three-by-five cards.
他当时就拿到了两张三乘五英寸的卡片。

39
00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.320
One said business school, and the other said bat in the office.
一张写着商学院，另一张写着办公室里的蝙蝠。

40
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.340
Well, look at that.
瞧瞧。

41
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.760
A succinct note card give.
真是简洁的卡片提示。

42
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:50.360
Yes.
没错。

43
00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.400
To go along with my succinct summary.
正好配合我那简洁的概要。

44
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.740
And I guess business school was Greg's idea.
我想商学院这个点子是格雷格想出来的。

45
00:01:54.980 --> 00:02:00.420
He always knew at some point down the road, he wanted to go to Ryan's business school.
他一直都知道，在未来的某个时刻，他想去瑞安的商学院看看。

46
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.700
And I guess that card had been on the wall for a while.
我想那张卡片在墙上已经贴了很久了。

47
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:09.100
Well, Angela, speaking of bat storylines, fast fact number one, Joss Whedon directed this episode.
好吧，安吉拉，说到蝙蝠的故事线，第一个速记事实，乔斯·韦登执导了这一集。

48
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:16.900
So, Joss is famous for creating Buffy the Vampire Slayer, the series starring Sarah Michelle Gellar.
乔斯因创作了由莎拉·米歇尔·盖拉主演的系列剧《吸血鬼猎人巴菲》而闻名。

49
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.640
This was a huge hit on the WB network, which was run at the time by Suzanne Daniels.
这是WB电视网的一部大热剧，当时由苏珊·丹尼尔斯管理。

50
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.400
Suzanne's husband is Greg Daniels.
苏珊的丈夫是格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

51
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:31.660
And that is how Joss kind of got his in to direct an episode of the show.
这就是乔斯得以执导本剧某一集的过程。

52
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:41.540
But I guess it is just a pure coincidence that he got assigned the episode with a bat and a vampire storyline.
但我猜他被分配到那一集正好有蝙蝠和吸血鬼的情节，纯属巧合。

53
00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.320
I remember he was like, come on, guys, you gave me the bat vampire story.
我记得他当时说，拜托，伙计们，你们竟然给了我这个蝙蝠吸血鬼的故事。

54
00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.780
And we're like, and everyone was like, it is pure coincidence.
我们当时就说，大家都在说，这纯属巧合。

55
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.800
Well, guys, we reached out to writer Brent Forrester.
好了，伙计们，我们联系了编剧布伦特·福雷斯特。

56
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.400
Remember, he sent in so many amazing audio clips for our grief counseling episode.
还记得吗，他在我们拍摄“悲伤辅导”那一集时发来了许多精彩的音频片段。

57
00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.320
He did it again this week.
这周他又发来了。

58
00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.720
And here's what he had to say about this.
以下是他对此事的看法。

59
00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:08.180
This episode was directed by Joss Whedon, who was a big, successful television creator at the time and happened to be a big fan of The Office.
这一集是由乔斯·韦登执导的，他当时是一位非常成功的大牌电视制作人，而且恰好是《办公室》的忠实粉丝。

60
00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.100
And he approached us asking if he could direct an episode.
他主动联系我们，询问是否可以执导其中一集。

61
00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.560
He ended up directing two, and this was the first one that he did.
他最终执导了两集，而这一集是他执导的第一集。

62
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:22.820
And it's just a total coincidence that the first episode that he directed happens to have a vampire subplot in it.
他执导的第一集里恰好有一个吸血鬼的副线情节，这完全是个巧合。

63
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.460
And he was the creator of Buffy the Vampire Slayer.
要知道他可是《吸血鬼猎人巴菲》的创作者。

64
00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:34.720
What you notice in that vampire subplot that I remember most is this visual detail that Joss added that was not in the script.
在那个吸血鬼副线情节中，我印象最深的是乔斯加入的一个剧本里没有的视觉细节。

65
00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:41.920
If you notice, at the end of the Jim Dwight vampire subplot, Jim says goodbye and leaves the office at the end of the day.
如果你注意看，在吉姆和德怀特的吸血鬼副线情节结尾，吉姆道别并在下班后离开了办公室。

66
00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:47.740
And when he does, he turns and he flips up his collar and sort of looks over his shoulder.
当他离开时，他转过身，竖起衣领，回头看了一眼。

67
00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:53.280
And it's the perfect image of Dracula looking over the corner of his cape.
那简直就是德古拉从斗篷角后窥视的完美画面。

68
00:03:53.600 --> 00:04:04.700
And it just works wonderfully as a visual gag, not in the script, totally the contribution of a guy who has worked a long time in the vampire genre.
这作为一个视觉笑话效果极佳，剧本里并没有这一段，完全是一位在吸血鬼题材领域深耕多年的创作者的贡献。

69
00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.240
That was pure Joss Whedon.
那完全是乔斯·韦登的风格。

70
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.060
I did not know that.
我之前不知道这一点。

71
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:08.980
I didn't know it either.
我也不知道。

72
00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:17.960
And you remember at this time, because I asked Kent Zabornak about this as well, he said that after season two, after we won the Emmy,
你还记得当时的情况吗？因为我也问过肯特·扎博纳克，他说在第二季之后，在我们赢得艾美奖之后，

73
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.360
we had a bunch of directors reaching out about directing our show.
有一大批导演主动联系我们，想要执导我们的剧集。

74
00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.240
Remember, like Harold Ramis, J.J.
记得吗，比如哈罗德·雷米斯、J.J.

75
00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:26.060
Abrams?
艾布拉姆斯？

76
00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.240
Jason Reitman?
杰森·雷特曼？

77
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.040
Yes.
没错。

78
00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.400
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

79
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.280
And Kent would just assign scripts according to director availability.
肯特只是根据导演的档期来分配剧本。

80
00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:38.680
And that is, he confirms, how Joss got this episode.
他证实，这就是乔斯拿到这一集的原因。

81
00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:44.260
So now, fast fact number two, location breakdown with Kentopedia.
现在，第二个速览事实，肯特百科之取景地解析。

82
00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:49.220
Ooh, we need a jingle for location breakdown with Kentopedia.
噢，我们需要为“肯特百科之取景地解析”配一段叮当声。

83
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.460
Location breakdown with Kentopedia.
肯特百科之取景地解析。

84
00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.320
Do you like it?
你喜欢吗？

85
00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:55.900
It's okay.
还行吧。

86
00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.000
I was trying to do like a schoolhouse rock thing.
我刚才试着模仿那种《摇滚学校》的风格。

87
00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.500
Yeah, I like it.
是的，我喜欢。

88
00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:00.160
Okay.
好吧。

89
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.380
Okay, location breakdown with Kentopedia.
好的，肯特百科之取景地解析。

90
00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.760
Is this about Northridge?
这是关于北岭分校的吗？

91
00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:04.560
Yes.
是的。

92
00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.520
We had a fan question.
我们收到一个粉丝提问。

93
00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:06.860
B.
B.

94
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:12.800
Smith, Major Tarwater, Julia Lee, Megan Meeker, Rose Cosette, and Tess Schmidt.
史密斯、塔沃特少校、朱莉娅·李、梅根·米克尔、罗斯·科塞特和苔丝·施密特。

95
00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:16.420
Where were the business school scenes shot in real life?
商学院的场景在现实中是在哪里拍摄的？

96
00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.420
Was it a real classroom on a campus?
那是校园里真实的教室吗？

97
00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.280
Were those real students or were they actors?
那些是真正的学生还是演员？

98
00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:29.740
Well, as Angela said, Ryan's business school and the scenes with Pam's art school were all shot at Cal State Northridge.
嗯，正如安吉拉所说，瑞恩的商学院场景和帕姆的艺术学校场景都是在加州州立大学北岭分校拍摄的。

99
00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.020
How did you know it was Cal State Northridge, Ange?
安吉，你是怎么知道那是加州州立大学北岭分校的？

100
00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.000
Because I listened to the DVD commentary.
因为我听了DVD评论音轨。

101
00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.420
Oh, y'all.
噢，大家伙儿。

102
00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:39.900
Well, Kent said all of the students in the classroom were hired extras,
肯特说教室里的学生全都是雇来的临时演员，

103
00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:47.880
that we used a total of 122 background actors that day for the classroom scenes and the exterior campus scenes.
那天我们一共用了122名背景演员来拍摄教室场景和校园外景。

104
00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:53.800
He said that the business school and the exterior scenes were filmed on day one.
他说商学院和外景是在第一天拍的。

105
00:05:53.800 --> 00:06:02.280
And on day two, we filmed the scenes for Pam's art show, which was held in the Cal State Northridge Design Center.
第二天我们拍了帕姆艺术展的戏份，是在加州州立大学北岭分校的设计中心拍的。

106
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:11.420
One of the things I liked that they talked about in the DVD commentary was Brent said they asked all the people playing students if they would please bring their own personal laptop.
DVD评论音轨里提到的一件事我很喜欢，布伦特说他们请求所有扮演学生的演员自带笔记本电脑。

107
00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:12.040
Oh.
噢。

108
00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.800
And when I watched the scene, Jenna, I noticed that all the laptops were different.
珍娜，我看那场戏的时候注意到，大家的笔记本电脑都不一样。

109
00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.340
That is such a good detail.
这细节真棒。

110
00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:19.580
All right.
好吧。

111
00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:20.840
Fast fact number three.
第三个冷知识。

112
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:21.160
Yeah.
嗯。

113
00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:27.520
Nine days after this episode aired, Rainn Wilson hosted Saturday Night Live.
这一集播出九天后，雷恩·威尔森主持了《周六夜现场》。

114
00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.920
Oh, you remember this?
噢，你还记得这个？

115
00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.300
Yes, we were so excited for him.
记得，我们当时都为他感到兴奋。

116
00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:36.500
So we had to kind of move around our shooting schedule to make this happen for Rainn.
为了成全雷恩，我们不得不调整了拍摄日程。

117
00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.720
And I just remember we were all so excited for him.
我记得我们当时都特别为他高兴。

118
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:46.980
And during his opening monologue, he did this bit, it's so funny, where he says,
在开场独白时，他演了一段特别好笑的戏，他说，

119
00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:52.280
Oh, he's just so excited to be at Saturday Night Live because it's just way more exciting than shooting The Office,
噢，他特别高兴能来《周六夜现场》，因为这比拍《办公室》刺激多了，

120
00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.360
which is basically just sitting at a desk on our fluorescent lights all day.
毕竟拍《办公室》整天就是坐在日光灯下的办公桌前。

121
00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:02.080
He was like, on the set of SNL, there's like scaffolding and there's props and there's costumes and wigs.
他说在《周六夜现场》的片场，有脚手架、道具、服装和假发。

122
00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.880
You know, it feels like a real show.
你知道，感觉就像个真正的节目。

123
00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.540
And he's like, let me show you, let me show you.
然后他说，我带你们看看，我带你们看看。

124
00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:10.860
And he takes the audience on like this backstage tour to show how exciting it is,
他带着观众在后台转了一圈，展示这里有多刺激，

125
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:19.920
only to find the cast of Saturday Night Live kind of dressed up doing impersonations of all of our characters from The Office.
结果发现《周六夜现场》的卡司们打扮成了我们《办公室》里所有角色的样子。

126
00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:20.580
Yes.
没错。

127
00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.360
Well, Kristen Wiig is Pam and she's answering phones.
克里斯汀·韦格扮演帕姆，正在接电话。

128
00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:24.440
Yes.
对。

129
00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.700
And he's like, hey, Kristen.
他说，嘿，克里斯汀。

130
00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:31.080
And she's like, SNL, hi, can I help you?
她说，SNL，您好，有什么能帮您的吗？

131
00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.380
She's like, I'm just answering phones.
她说，我就是在接电话。

132
00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:34.580
And he's like, what are you doing?
他说，你在干什么呢？

133
00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.940
She's like, I do this all the time.
她说，我平时就干这个。

134
00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.400
I do a lot of things.
我还会做很多事。

135
00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:38.820
He's like, don't you do anything else?
他说，你就没别的事做吗？

136
00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.540
And she's like, well, I also like to paint.
她说，嗯，我还喜欢画画。

137
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:46.120
And then she holds up a watercolor painting of 30 Rockefeller Center.
然后她举起了一幅洛克菲勒中心30号的水彩画。

138
00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.720
That's where they film SNL.
那是他们拍摄《周六夜现场》的地方。

139
00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:56.680
And that is a callback to this episode that had just aired of Pam's watercolor of Dunder Mifflin.
这呼应了刚刚播出的这一集里帕姆画的那幅邓德·米福林水彩画。

140
00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:01.200
And I was freaking out excited when I saw it.
我看到的时候简直激动坏了。

141
00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.860
Amy Poehler played me.
艾米·波勒演了我。

142
00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:03.920
Oh, it's so funny.
噢，太搞笑了。

143
00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.700
And like had this like sort of like snarl and like kind of flirted with Rain as Dwight.
她还带着那种坏笑，像德怀特一样跟雷恩调情。

144
00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:14.520
And if you remember, Jenna, Rashida was there that weekend and she's friends with a lot of the SNL cast members.
珍娜，你还记得吗，那个周末拉什达也在，她和《周六夜现场》的很多卡司都是朋友。

145
00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.520
So they were like, just hop in as Karen.
所以他们就说，你也来演凯伦吧。

146
00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.000
So she did.
于是她就去了。

147
00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.480
He walks down the hall.
他走在走廊里。

148
00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.920
And they took all these pictures and Rashida emailed them to me.
他们拍了好多照片，拉什达发邮件给我了。

149
00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.360
She was like, Ange, look, it's Amy is you.
她说，安吉，你看，艾米演的是你。

150
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:29.460
And I have all of these great pictures of them from the set that day.
我留着那天他们在片场拍的所有精彩照片。

151
00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:30.580
Amazing.
太棒了。

152
00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:31.880
Are you going to put those on the pod?
你要把那些照片发到播客上吗？

153
00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.060
On Office League's pod?
发到《办公室联盟》的播客上？

154
00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:33.920
Yes, I'll put one.
是的，我会发一张。

155
00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:34.940
I have a great one.
我有一张很棒的照片。

156
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.920
I think I have a group shot I'll put on the pod.
我想我有一张合影，我会发到播客上。

157
00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:40.700
Well, listen to what Kristen Wiig did after that episode aired.
听听克里斯汀·韦格在那集播出后做了什么。

158
00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:41.140
What?
什么？

159
00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:44.260
So she and I shared a manager and we'd met a few times.
当时我和她共用一个经纪人，我们见过几次面。

160
00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:48.100
We were both really struggling actresses at the same time.
我们当时都是在苦苦挣扎的女演员。

161
00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.340
And kind of when I got on The Office, she got on Saturday Night Live.
后来我进了《办公室》，她进了《周六夜现场》。

162
00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.960
So this was really thrilling to us.
所以这对我们来说真的很令人激动。

163
00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.520
I get a package in the mail.
我收到一个邮包。

164
00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:59.360
It is the watercolor that she held up on the show.
里面就是她在节目里举着的那幅水彩画。

165
00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.220
She signed the back of it.
她在背面签了名。

166
00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:06.380
And then she wrote me the nicest note that was just like, I just know what it would mean
还给我写了一张特别暖心的字条，大意是，我太了解如果我能在电视节目里被模仿，

167
00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:11.860
to me if I were ever parodied on this television show.
那对我意味着什么。

168
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.840
And I thought you might like to have a prop from the moment.
我想你可能想留着这个拍摄道具作为纪念。

169
00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.380
So I asked if I could send this to you.
所以我问他们能不能把这个寄给你。

170
00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.380
And they said yes.
他们答应了。

171
00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.880
That is so lovely.
那真是太贴心了。

172
00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:20.620
Yeah.
是啊。

173
00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.600
And I have it framed and it's in my family room.
我把它装裱起来，挂在我的家庭活动室里。

174
00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.700
That is so great, Jenna.
那太棒了，珍娜。

175
00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:26.780
I never knew that.
我以前都不知道。

176
00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.880
I've been in your family room a gazillion times.
我去过你家家庭活动室无数次了。

177
00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:29.840
Yeah.
是啊。

178
00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:33.700
It's up on the shelf with the Simpsons cartoon that Greg made of us.
它就放在架子上，和格雷格为我们画的那张《辛普森一家》风格的漫画放在一起。

179
00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.040
This is like my two treasured iteMs.
这两样东西是我最珍视的收藏。

180
00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.100
I'm going to look for it next time I'm at your house.
下次去你家我一定要找找看。

181
00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:39.880
She's the best, guys.
她真是太好了，伙计们。

182
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.220
That is so sweet.
太暖心了。

183
00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.260
Well, listen, that's all I got.
好了，听着，我就这些要说的。

184
00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:47.660
I think we should go to a break and then we'll come back and talk all about business school
我觉得我们该休息一下了，回来后我们要聊聊《商学院》这一集，

185
00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:53.720
with a bunch of great audio clips from Brent and a little special surprise from Kate Flannery.
还会播放布伦特的一些精彩音频片段，以及凯特·弗兰纳里带来的特别惊喜。

186
00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:54.440
Yes.
好的。

187
00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.320
We'll see you.
待会儿见。

188
00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:56.120
Okay.
好的。

189
00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:07.830
We are back and let's get into this episode.
我们回来了，让我们开始聊这一集吧。

190
00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:13.870
You guys, we start with Kevin arriving a little late to work and he says he almost died because
伙计们，开头是凯文上班迟到了，他说他差点就死了，因为

191
00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:14.790
his tire blew out.
他的轮胎爆了。

192
00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:15.890
Michael doesn't care.
迈克尔根本不在乎。

193
00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:16.930
He doesn't care.
他一点都不在乎。

194
00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:21.070
He just keeps saying, why is today a special day?
他一直问，为什么今天是个特别的日子？

195
00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:26.630
And Jenna, when he said, pop quiz, all I could think about was Keanu Reeves.
珍娜，当他说“突击测验”时，我满脑子想的都是基努·里维斯。

196
00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.140
Why?
为什么？

197
00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.480
Because of speed.
因为《生死时速》啊。

198
00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:31.380
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

199
00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:32.740
Pop quiz, asshole.
突击测验，混蛋。

200
00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.700
You have a hair trigger aimed at your head.
你的脑袋上正顶着一把一触即发的枪。

201
00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.020
What do you do?
你是做什么工作的？

202
00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:38.260
What do you do?
你是做什么工作的？

203
00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.420
When's the last time you watched this movie?
你上次看这部电影是什么时候？

204
00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:41.400
Three days ago.
三天前。

205
00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.940
Well, I see now why you made the connection.
好吧，我现在明白你为什么会联想到这一出了。

206
00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:45.820
I know.
我知道。

207
00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:49.420
I'm really sad Michael didn't do a Keanu Reeves impression in this moment.
我真的很遗憾迈克尔在这儿没模仿一下基努·里维斯。

208
00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.180
Oh, well, that's a missed opportunity.
噢，那真是错失良机。

209
00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:52.650
I know.
我知道。

210
00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:54.060
That would have been full circle for me.
那对我来说就圆满了。

211
00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.220
It would have made me very happy.
那会让我非常开心。

212
00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.080
But yeah.
不过确实。

213
00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.600
I remember shooting this scene.
我记得拍这场戏的时候。

214
00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:58.320
Yeah.
是啊。

215
00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.220
And here's my problem.
这就是我的问题所在。

216
00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:10.460
Whenever they would put Brian Baumgartner by reception to do anything Kevin, especially
每当他们让布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳坐在前台去演凯文的戏份，尤其是

217
00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:15.940
Kevin with like hurt feelings, I can't keep it together.
那种受了委屈的凯文，我就忍不住笑场。

218
00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:20.040
I can't look at him when he is doing sad Kevin.
他演伤心的凯文时，我根本不敢看他。

219
00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:21.500
I can't.
我真的不行。

220
00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:23.200
So funny.
太搞笑了。

221
00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:30.560
Well, Michael's excited because he gets to go to Ryan's business school and he's so happy.
迈克尔很兴奋，因为他要去瑞安的商学院了，他特别高兴。

222
00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:35.640
And we have a Ryan talking head where he's like, look, I get to go up a whole letter grade
我们还有一段瑞安的采访，他说，看，如果我带老板去，

223
00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:36.820
if I bring my boss in.
我的成绩就能提高一个等级。

224
00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:37.880
I should.
我应该去。

225
00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:38.200
Yeah.
是啊。

226
00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.220
I should do it.
我应该这么做。

227
00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:39.500
Right.
对吧。

228
00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:41.840
No.
不。

229
00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.520
No, you shouldn't, Ryan.
不，你不应该，瑞安。

230
00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:47.620
And yeah, well, we're going to see maybe no, you shouldn't.
是啊，好吧，我们待会儿会看到，也许不，你不应该去。

231
00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:51.560
But Michael is just thrilled.
但迈克尔简直乐坏了。

232
00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.120
We have a scene where Dwight is helping him pack.
我们有一场戏是德怀特帮他打包行李。

233
00:11:55.680 --> 00:12:02.960
And this leads us to one of my favorite Dwight talking heads, which is a famous talking head.
这引出了我最喜欢的德怀特采访片段之一，那可是个名场面。

234
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.480
It is one of my favorite.
那是我最喜欢的片段之一。

235
00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.600
My kids love this talking head so much, Jenna.
我的孩子们特别喜欢这个采访片段，珍娜。

236
00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.440
Michael's asking him, what is the best advice I ever gave you?
迈克尔问他，我给过你最好的建议是什么？

237
00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:16.440
And Dwight's like, the best advice you ever gave me, Michael, is don't be an idiot.
德怀特说，迈克尔，你给过我最好的建议就是别做个白痴。

238
00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:18.060
It changed my life.
它改变了我的人生。

239
00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:24.200
And then it cuts to this famous, amazing talking head where Dwight looks at Cameron says,
然后镜头切到了这个著名又精彩的采访片段，德怀特看着镜头说，

240
00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:29.100
whenever I'm about to do something, I think, would an idiot do that?
每当我准备做某事时，我都会想，白痴会做这件事吗？

241
00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.660
And if they would, I do not do that thing.
如果他们会做，那我就不做那件事。

242
00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:32.840
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

243
00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:40.340
I just wrote out a birthday card to a young woman who was turning 21, and I put this in her card.
我刚给一个快满21岁的年轻女孩写了张生日贺卡，我就把这句话写进去了。

244
00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:49.700
I said, listen, as you move on to this next phase of adulthood, remember these wise words from Dwight Schrute.
我说，听着，当你迈向成年的下一个阶段时，记住德怀特·施鲁特的这些至理名言。

245
00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.640
Yes, that is so good.
没错，这太棒了。

246
00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.380
So I use this all the time.
所以我经常用这句话。

247
00:12:55.420 --> 00:13:03.620
So then Michael's in the car with Ryan, and he's like, man, do you think people are going to throw their hats in the air after my speech?
然后迈克尔和瑞安在车里，他说，伙计，你觉得大家在我演讲后会把帽子扔向空中吗？

248
00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:08.320
You know, because they do that sometimes in graduations or at naval academies.
你知道的，因为他们在毕业典礼或海军学院有时会那样做。

249
00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.620
And Ryan's like, yeah, this is, I don't, this is just, it's not that.
瑞安说，是啊，这，我不知道，这只是，这不是那种场合。

250
00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:14.620
It's not that occasion.
那不是那种场合。

251
00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:18.120
I loved this actual line from Ryan.
我特别喜欢瑞安这句台词。

252
00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:23.460
Jenna made me laugh out loud because he says, you understand no one is graduating.
珍娜让我笑出声来，因为他说，你要明白没人能毕业。

253
00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:36.660
And you've got to know Ryan is now crapping in his pants because he's like, he has a line prepared if they throw their hats.
你得知道瑞安当时吓得要死，因为他准备了一句台词，以防他们把帽子扔向空中。

254
00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:38.500
And this is the line.
就是这句台词。

255
00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.720
May your hats fly as high as your dreaMs.
愿你们的帽子飞得像你们的梦想一样高。

256
00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:47.400
And I have seen people put that on their graduation hats for graduations.
我见过有人把这句话写在毕业帽上。

257
00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:48.720
I have too.
我也见过。

258
00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.440
So now we go back to the office.
现在我们回到办公室。

259
00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:57.460
And this is when we learn about Pam's art show because Roy says he's really excited.
这时我们得知了帕姆的艺术展，因为罗伊说他非常兴奋。

260
00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:00.840
We have back to back really awkward Pam and Jim talking heads.
接着是帕姆和吉姆接连不断的尴尬访谈。

261
00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:01.320
Yeah.
是啊。

262
00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.220
Pam's like, I'm happy to be with Roy.
帕姆说，我很高兴能和罗伊在一起。

263
00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.520
And then Jim's like, yeah, Pam's with Roy.
然后吉姆说，是啊，帕姆和罗伊在一起。

264
00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.360
I'm with Kevin.
我和凯文在一起。

265
00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:07.000
Moving on.
继续吧。

266
00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.440
And just like, okay, guys.
就像是，好吧，伙计们。

267
00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.540
I think he's with Karen.
我想他是和凯伦在一起。

268
00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:10.300
Who would I say?
我刚才说了谁？

269
00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:11.340
Kevin.
凯文。

270
00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:12.700
No, I didn't.
不，我没说。

271
00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:13.500
You did.
你说了。

272
00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.740
And everyone listening right now just heard you say, oh, no.
现在所有听众都听见你说了，哦，不。

273
00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:18.800
Maybe I should take a sip of my tea.
也许我该喝口茶。

274
00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:20.560
Maybe I need more caffeine this morning.
也许我今天早上需要更多咖啡因。

275
00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.260
Wake yourself up.
让自己清醒点。

276
00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.440
You were up late last night.
你昨晚熬夜了。

277
00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.080
I was, lady.
我是熬夜了，女士。

278
00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.080
I was.
确实。

279
00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:31.660
I know because I woke up to a string of messages from you that were sent at like 1230 in the morning.
我知道，因为我醒来时看到你发来的一连串消息，大概是凌晨12点半发的。

280
00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:32.020
I'm so sorry.
真抱歉。

281
00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.720
I didn't think you like, what is it?
我没想到你会，怎么说呢？

282
00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:34.860
Does it alert you or something?
它会提醒你什么的吗？

283
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:35.640
I have my alert.
我有开启提醒。

284
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.120
No, no.
不，不。

285
00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.500
It was when I woke up.
是我醒来的时候看到的。

286
00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:40.740
I woke up and looked at my phone and I was like, wow.
我醒来一看手机，心想，哇。

287
00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:45.820
Because I woke up really early this morning and I was shocked to see all these messages from you.
因为我今天起得特别早，看到你发来的这些消息我很惊讶。

288
00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:48.500
I was like, wow, Angela's a real early bird today, too.
我心想，哇，安吉拉今天也是个早起鸟啊。

289
00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:49.320
Look at us.
看看我们。

290
00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.540
And I was like, no, they were from late last night.
然后我才反应过来，不，那是昨晚很晚发的。

291
00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.000
Yeah, they were from really late last night.
是啊，那是昨晚很晚发的。

292
00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.200
I wasn't up being an idiot.
我不是在熬夜做傻事。

293
00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.100
I was, I was working.
我是在工作。

294
00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:58.020
Jenna and I, you know, we have some other stuff.
我和珍娜，你知道，我们还有些别的事情。

295
00:14:58.240 --> 00:14:59.460
I didn't say you were up being an idiot.
我没说你在熬夜做傻事。

296
00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.020
No, I know.
不，我知道。

297
00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:02.100
I'm telling the 21-year-olds out there.
我是对那些21岁的年轻人说的。

298
00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:05.140
Jenna and I have some other stuff, guys, that we're hatching up.
我和珍娜还有些别的事情在筹划，伙计们。

299
00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.640
And I was working on one of them.
我当时就是在忙其中一件。

300
00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:07.840
We have something brewing.
我们正在酝酿一些事情。

301
00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.980
I was inspired late last night.
我昨晚深夜灵感迸发。

302
00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:10.440
Okay.
好的。

303
00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:11.100
I like it.
我很喜欢。

304
00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.040
I've had a cup of tea.
我喝了杯茶。

305
00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.260
I'm waking myself up.
我正在让自己清醒过来。

306
00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.020
I'm not going to call Karen Kevin.
我可不会管凯伦叫凯文。

307
00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:18.540
So now Pam tells Kelly about her art show.
现在帕姆告诉凯莉关于她艺术展的事。

308
00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:25.180
Mindy's performance, where she feigns interest and acts like she's going to come, is just freaking amazing.
敏迪的表演简直太绝了，她假装很感兴趣，表现得好像她会去一样。

309
00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.120
It's perfect.
太完美了。

310
00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:26.420
Yeah.
是啊。

311
00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:32.740
It's all of us when we've been invited to something that we know we're not going to go to, but we're saying we're going to go to it.
这就像我们所有人被邀请参加某个明知不会去，却还是答应会去的活动时的样子。

312
00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:33.960
Yeah.
没错。

313
00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.060
Oh, I would.
哦，我会去的。

314
00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:35.400
Yes.
好的。

315
00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:36.000
Yes.
没问题。

316
00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:38.900
I will absolutely be there.
我绝对会到场。

317
00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:40.020
Yes.
好的。

318
00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:41.160
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

319
00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:41.980
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

320
00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:42.800
All right.
好吧。

321
00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:45.900
So now Michael arrives on campus.
现在迈克尔到达了校园。

322
00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.940
He is so excited.
他非常兴奋。

323
00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:55.680
There's just all of these memories coming back to him that he's having that might have occurred if he had ever attended college.
他脑海中涌现出各种回忆，仿佛他真的上过大学一样。

324
00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.820
That made me sad, by the way.
顺便说一句，那让我感到难过。

325
00:15:57.980 --> 00:15:59.640
It made me sad, too.
我也觉得很难过。

326
00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:01.560
I mean, Michael would have loved college.
我是说，迈克尔一定会喜欢大学生活的。

327
00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:05.180
I think Michael would have been like an RA in the dorm, you know?
我觉得迈克尔会成为那种宿舍管理员，你懂的吧？

328
00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:06.080
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

329
00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.480
And he probably would have been like a lifer RA.
而且他可能会当一辈子的宿舍管理员。

330
00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:10.300
They probably would have been like, you can leave now.
校方可能会说，你可以走了。

331
00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.680
And he's like, no, we got another batch of students coming in.
而他会说，不，还有一批新学生要来了。

332
00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.380
And they're like, you're not a student anymore.
然后他们会说，你已经不是学生了。

333
00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:15.560
Yeah.
是啊。

334
00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.340
Yeah, that's true.
没错，确实如此。

335
00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:19.280
It's true.
是真的。

336
00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:23.400
Well, we had a fan comment from Amber Morris.
对了，我们收到了一条来自安珀·莫里斯的粉丝评论。

337
00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:23.780
Okay.
好的。

338
00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:29.160
You know that moment when Michael runs up and tries to join the Frisbee game?
你记得迈克尔跑过去试图加入飞盘游戏的那一刻吗？

339
00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:29.520
Yeah.
记得。

340
00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:32.240
She says, fun fast fact.
她说，分享一个有趣的冷知识。

341
00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:37.440
A friend of mine, Nathan Blank, played the Frisbee student at Ryan's school.
我的一个朋友内森·布兰克，在瑞安的学校里扮演了那个玩飞盘的学生。

342
00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:40.740
Michael ran up and stole a Frisbee and threw it.
迈克尔跑过来抢走飞盘并把它扔了出去。

343
00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:43.380
And Nathan's line was something like, dude.
内森的台词大概就是，哥们儿。

344
00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:49.740
And he has had nothing but wonderful things to say about his filming day and working with Steve and BJ.
他说起拍摄那天以及和史蒂夫、BJ合作的经历，全是溢美之词。

345
00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.760
Aw, I love that.
噢，我喜欢这个。

346
00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:52.720
Yeah.
是啊。

347
00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:53.760
That is very sweet.
那真是太贴心了。

348
00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:59.140
That scene made me laugh really hard because everything about how Steve approached that Frisbee was wrong.
那场戏让我笑得不行，因为史蒂夫处理那个飞盘的方式从头到尾都不对劲。

349
00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:02.600
No one should ever grab a Frisbee and throw it that way.
没人应该那样去抓飞盘并扔出去。

350
00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:04.940
And it just was so perfect.
那场戏简直太完美了。

351
00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:09.200
Well, now we're going to go back to the office, Angela.
好了，现在我们要回到办公室了，安吉拉。

352
00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:16.860
Because now that other card that Brent talked about, the one that says bad in office, is about to go into play.
因为布伦特提到的那张卡片，就是写着办公室里有坏东西的那张，马上就要派上用场了。

353
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.040
We're in the office.
我们现在在办公室里。

354
00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:20.860
Dwight sees some kind of animal feces.
德怀特看到了一些动物粪便。

355
00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.100
He's on the case.
他开始调查了。

356
00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:26.900
He's like, oh, there's a bird in the rafters, guys.
他说，噢，伙计们，房梁上有只鸟。

357
00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:28.660
But it's not a bird.
但那不是鸟。

358
00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:29.460
It's a bat.
是只蝙蝠。

359
00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.600
And everyone freaks out.
大家都吓坏了。

360
00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.260
Everyone except Jim and Creed.
除了吉姆和克里德。

361
00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:34.920
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

362
00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:35.680
Creed is ready.
克里德已经准备好了。

363
00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.780
Angela stops, drops, and rolls.
安吉拉停下脚步，趴下并开始翻滚。

364
00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:39.160
Yeah.
没错。

365
00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.640
Stanley leaves.
斯坦利离开了。

366
00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:45.680
Eventually, Dwight is able to lock the bat in the conference room after a bunch of mayhem.
最终，在一阵混乱之后，德怀特成功把蝙蝠锁在了会议室里。

367
00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:51.680
Fan question from Leona Woldridge, Ruth Rodriguez, Heather Flynn, and Abby Mole.
来自莱奥娜·沃尔德里奇、露丝·罗德里格斯、希瑟·弗林和艾比·莫尔的粉丝提问。

368
00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:56.600
At approximately five minutes, Angela drops and rolls while the bat flies around.
在大约五分钟的时候，当蝙蝠到处乱飞时，安吉拉趴下并翻滚了。

369
00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:02.260
Then you barely hear her voice in the background, either talking to herself or praying.
然后你几乎听不到她在背景里的声音，要么是在自言自语，要么是在祈祷。

370
00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:03.260
Do you know what you're saying?
你知道你在说什么吗？

371
00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:03.640
I do.
我知道。

372
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:08.080
I remember Joss saying to me, all right, Angela would totally freak out.
我记得乔斯对我说，好吧，安吉拉肯定会彻底吓坏的。

373
00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.860
And, you know, we talked about what did that look like?
然后，你知道，我们讨论过那看起来会是什么样？

374
00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.480
And what I dropped to the ground.
还有我趴到地上的样子。

375
00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:17.140
And I came up with this dropping to the ground and rolling.
我想出了这个趴到地上并翻滚的动作。

376
00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.940
That's my memory, Jenna.
那是我的记忆，珍娜。

377
00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.880
That I dropped to the ground and I decided to roll.
我趴到了地上，然后决定翻滚。

378
00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.780
And Joss really liked that.
乔斯真的很喜欢那个动作。

379
00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:26.060
And then I just laid face down on the carpet.
然后我就脸朝下趴在地毯上。

380
00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.740
And I improvised this.
我即兴发挥了这一点。

381
00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:31.060
And I said something like, God, this is Angela Martin.
我说了一些类似的话，上帝啊，我是安吉拉·马丁。

382
00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:34.700
Please don't let that stupid thing come anywhere near me.
请别让那该死的东西靠近我。

383
00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.820
And I just sort of mumbled these prayers.
我就那样嘟囔着这些祈祷词。

384
00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:37.940
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

385
00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:44.940
When I was a child and I would pray, I would lead with, God, this is Jenna Fisher.
我小时候祈祷时，开头会说，上帝啊，我是珍娜·费舍尔。

386
00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.420
I would lead with an introduction.
我会先做一个自我介绍。

387
00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:48.480
Same.
我也是。

388
00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:49.760
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

389
00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:50.020
Yeah.
没错。

390
00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:55.680
I was like, well, I need God to know, like, I need him to like key into who are these prayers
我当时想，好吧，我需要上帝知道，就是，我需要他能锁定这些祈祷是

391
00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:56.000
for?
给谁的？

392
00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:59.900
As I'm receiving these prayers, who are they coming from?
当我收到这些祈祷时，它们是谁发来的？

393
00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.840
So I thought, well, I'll lead with my name.
所以我心想，好吧，我得先报上我的名字。

394
00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:04.880
I used to say, Lord God, this is Angela Kinsey.
我过去常说，主啊，我是安吉拉·金赛。

395
00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.060
I'm in my bedroom.
我在我的卧室里。

396
00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:10.880
I am on a street called Kavling in Jakarta, Indonesia.
我在印度尼西亚雅加达一条叫卡夫林的街道上。

397
00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.460
That is in the Southern Hemisphere.
那是在南半球。

398
00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:15.720
It's a group of islands.
那是一群岛屿。

399
00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:17.660
I'm just below the equator.
我刚好在赤道下方。

400
00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.420
Like I needed him to know where I was.
就像我需要让他知道我在哪里一样。

401
00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:25.720
That was some serious location honing right there.
刚才那段定位真是太精准了。

402
00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.780
You were like, the coordinates are.
你当时就像是说，坐标是。

403
00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:28.020
Yes.
没错。

404
00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:28.540
Latitude.
纬度。

405
00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:30.360
75 degrees latitude.
北纬75度。

406
00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:33.140
I'm in my bedroom.
我就在卧室里。

407
00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:34.600
It's down the hall on the right.
就在走廊尽头右边。

408
00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:37.420
It's across from the bathroom.
在浴室对面。

409
00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:38.680
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

410
00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:43.000
I did not get that specific, but I applaud that.
我没说得那么具体，但我为你鼓掌。

411
00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:43.320
Thank you.
谢谢。

412
00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:46.220
Then we had more fan questions about this scene.
接下来我们还有更多粉丝关于这一幕的提问。

413
00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:52.840
From Rosalie W., Tanner W., Mia F., and Jacob W.
来自Rosalie W.、Tanner W.、Mia F.和Jacob W.。

414
00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:56.560
Was the bat that got trapped in the office a real bat?
办公室里那只被困住的蝙蝠是真的吗？

415
00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:58.880
Kent, Kentapedia, says.
Kent，也就是“Kent百科”，说。

416
00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:00.460
Yes.
是的。

417
00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:03.440
We used a real bat for three scenes.
我们在三个场景里用了真蝙蝠。

418
00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:08.040
The scene where Dwight stands on Pam's reception desk to look inside the ceiling.
Dwight站在Pam的前台桌子上往天花板里看的那场戏。

419
00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:12.200
A few shots of the bat on the ceiling in the conference room.
会议室天花板上蝙蝠的几个镜头。

420
00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:16.020
And for that shot of the bat on the ceiling in the kitchen.
还有厨房天花板上蝙蝠的那个镜头。

421
00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:21.220
Kent hired two bat wranglers to provide us with the bat, Chad Dunn and John Baldwin.
Kent雇了两位蝙蝠驯兽师来提供蝙蝠，分别是Chad Dunn和John Baldwin。

422
00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:27.980
And they put Chad up in the ceiling to hold the bat for that scene where Dwight peers in.
在Dwight往里看的那场戏里，他们把Chad送进天花板里抓着蝙蝠。

423
00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:30.260
The one we were just talking about.
就是我们刚才说的那场戏。

424
00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:34.840
Now, the rest of the time when we see the bat flying around, that was all CGI.
至于剩下的时间里我们看到的蝙蝠飞来飞去，那全是电脑特效。

425
00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:39.840
Kent said he hired Mitch Suskin as our visual effects supervisor.
Kent说他雇了Mitch Suskin担任我们的视觉特效总监。

426
00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.960
He was great, did a terrific job.
他很棒，工作做得非常出色。

427
00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:45.800
And they worked with several production houses to animate the bat.
他们还与几家制作公司合作完成了蝙蝠的动画制作。

428
00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:53.360
And then there was a third kind of bat that we used, which we will talk about later in the scene with Kate.
此外我们还用了第三种蝙蝠，稍后在Kate的那场戏里我们会讲到。

429
00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:56.060
And it was a mechanical bat.
那是一只机械蝙蝠。

430
00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:56.520
Yes.
没错。

431
00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:58.460
So three different bats.
所以一共用了三种不同的蝙蝠。

432
00:20:58.700 --> 00:20:59.140
Three different bats.
三种不同的蝙蝠。

433
00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.180
I have a tiny bit of bat trivia.
我有一点关于蝙蝠的小知识。

434
00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:02.700
Oh, lay it on me.
哦，说来听听。

435
00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:02.980
Okay.
好的。

436
00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.900
Here's my little bit of bat trivia from this episode.
这是我从这一集中搜集到的关于蝙蝠的小知识。

437
00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:09.920
In the DVD commentary, Rain says he named the bat.
在DVD评论音轨里，Rain说他给那只蝙蝠取了名字。

438
00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:12.520
That he was talking to the bat wrangler.
当时他正在和蝙蝠驯兽师聊天。

439
00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:14.620
And Rain said, what's his name?
Rain问，它叫什么名字？

440
00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:18.280
And the bat wrangler was like, oh, we've never given him a name.
驯兽师说，哦，我们从来没给它取过名字。

441
00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:19.400
And Rain was like, what?
Rain就说，什么？

442
00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:21.280
I'm going to name him.
我要给它取个名字。

443
00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:24.300
And so Rain named the bat Gary.
于是Rain给那只蝙蝠取名叫Gary。

444
00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:26.840
It's Gary the bat.
就是Gary蝙蝠。

445
00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:28.520
And we called him Gary all week.
那一整周我们都叫它Gary。

446
00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:30.880
Well, good job, Gary.
好吧，干得好，Gary。

447
00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:31.320
Yeah.
是啊。

448
00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:37.300
And now my question is, Rain, if you ever listen to this, is that Michael Gary, Scott?
现在我的问题是，Rain，如果你哪天听到这个，它是取自Michael Gary Scott吗？

449
00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:39.300
Oh.
哦。

450
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.280
